                        'kunya' => 'Abu Usamah',
                        'laqab' => 'Hibb Rasulillah (the Beloved of the Messenger of Allah)',
                        'biography' => "Zayd ibn Harithah, the beloved freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, is the only companion named in the Quran: 'So when Zayd had no longer any need for her...' (33:37). Captured as a boy from his tribe of Kalb, he was bought by Khadijah and gifted to the Prophet before the revelation. When his father and uncle came to ransom him, the Prophet let him choose — and Zayd chose to stay, saying, 'I would never choose anyone over you; you are to me as father and uncle.' The Prophet freed him and adopted him by the custom of the age, so he was called Zayd ibn Muhammad until the verse 'Call them by their fathers' was revealed. He was among the very first to embrace Islam — the first freedman to believe. In Medina the Prophet paired him in brotherhood with Hamza. He fought at Badr, the Trench and the other campaigns; the Prophet married him to Umm Ayman, who bore Usamah — 'the beloved, son of the beloved' — and later to his own cousin Zaynab bint Jahsh. Aisha said: 'The Messenger of Allah never sent Zayd on an expedition except as its commander; had he outlived him, he would have made him his successor.' In Jumada al-Ula 8 AH the Prophet placed him at the head of the army of Mu'tah against the Byzantines, saying: 'If Zayd is killed, then Ja'far; if Ja'far is killed, then Abdullah ibn Rawahah.' Zayd fought bearing the Prophet's banner until the spears took him, the first of the three martyred commanders, whom the Prophet — his eyes flowing — announced had been raised to him in Paradise.",
                        'virtues' => "The Prophet's beloved and freedman, the only companion named in the Quran. He chose the Prophet over his own father and family. Never sent on an expedition except as its commander; Aisha said the Prophet would have made him his successor had he lived.",
                        'famous_narrations' => null,
                        'martyrdom' => "Zayd was martyred at Mu'tah in Jumada al-Ula 8 AH as first commander of the army, appointed by the Prophet ﷺ himself. Bearing the Prophet's banner against the Byzantine host, he fought until cut down by spears; Ja'far ibn Abi Talib and then Abdullah ibn Rawahah took the banner and followed him in martyrdom. In Medina, before any news arrived, the Prophet announced their deaths with tears flowing, saying they had been raised to him in Paradise.",
